# =============================================================================
# deploy/.dockerignore — NOTE: this file is NOT the one Docker uses.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The build context is the REPO ROOT (`build.context: ..` in
# deploy/docker-compose.yml, and `docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .`), so the
# authoritative ignore file is the repository-root `/.dockerignore`.
#
# Docker only reads `.dockerignore` at the root of the build context, never next
# to the Dockerfile. This file exists so anyone looking for an ignore file next
# to deploy/Dockerfile finds this explanation instead of a wrong guess; it is
# intentionally comment-only (an empty pattern set) and harmless.
#
# Do not build with `docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile deploy/`: the Dockerfile
# COPYs scorer/* from the context, which does not exist under deploy/.
#
# See: ../../.dockerignore (repo root)
# =============================================================================
